/-
# Varieties generated by finitely based quasivarieties (Kourovka Notebook Problem 8.28)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.28 (A. V. Kuznetsov): is the variety of
groups finitely based if it is generated by a finitely based quasivariety of groups?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.FormationVarietyPGroupsKourovka11Problem21Wanted
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FinitelyBasedQuasivarietyVarietyKourovka8Problem28Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 8.28 (A. V.
Kuznetsov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700480 (`KOU-8.28`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Quasi-identities and their models are `QuasiIdentity` and `Models` from
`WantedExt/GroupTheory/QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted.lean`; a
finitely based quasivariety is the class of models of a finite set `Q` of quasi-identities. The
variety it generates has as laws the words of `FreeGroup ℕ` that are laws of every model; it is
finitely based when finitely many words define it (`SatisfiesLaws` from
`WantedExt/GroupTheory/FormationVarietyPGroupsKourovka11Problem21Wanted.lean`).
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FormationVarietyPGroupsKourovka11Problem21Wanted
open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.QuasivarietyMaximalSubquasivarietiesKourovka14Problem25Wanted

/-- The laws of the variety generated by the quasivariety of models of `Q`: the words of
`FreeGroup ℕ` that are laws of every group satisfying all quasi-identities of `Q`. -/
def generatedLaws (Q : Set QuasiIdentity) : Set (FreeGroup ℕ) :=
  {w | ∀ (H : Type) [Group H], Models Q H → ∀ f : FreeGroup ℕ →* H, f w = 1}

/-- The variety with set of laws `L` is finitely based: finitely many words `S` define it, that
is, a group satisfies all laws of `L` exactly when it satisfies the words of `S`. -/
def IsFinitelyBased (L : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) : Prop :=
  ∃ S : Finset (FreeGroup ℕ), ∀ (K : Type) [Group K],
    SatisfiesLaws L K ↔ SatisfiesLaws (S : Set (FreeGroup ℕ)) K

/-- Kourovka 8.28 (A. V. Kuznetsov): the variety generated by a finitely based quasivariety of
groups (the models of finitely many quasi-identities) is finitely based. -/
def finitelyBasedQuasivarietyGeneratesFinitelyBased : Prop :=
  ∀ Q : Set QuasiIdentity, Q.Finite → IsFinitelyBased (generatedLaws Q)

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 8.28 "No, not always", citing Anokhin (1998), who
constructs soluble finitely based quasivarieties of groups (of derived length at most `7`) that
generate non-finitely based varieties. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 8.28 (A. V. Kuznetsov); resolution: M. I. Anokhin, A basis of identities of
a variety generated by a finitely-based quasi-variety of groups, Sb. Math. 189 (1998), 1115-1124,
Kourovka Archive, Problem 8.28: No, not always; paper, Theorem 1 and abstract: soluble finitely
based quasivarieties of groups that generate non-finitely based varieties,
https://doi.org/10.1070/SM1998v189n08ABEH000330.
-/
public theorem_wanted finitelyBasedQuasivarietyGeneratesFinitelyBased_refuted :
    ¬ finitelyBasedQuasivarietyGeneratesFinitelyBased

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.FinitelyBasedQuasivarietyVarietyKourovka8Problem28Wanted
